      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city of Rochester was incorporated in 1967, and the rest of Avon Township became Rochester Hills in 1984.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rochester_Hills%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When voters chose the city’s name, Rochester Hills won by a landslide over the alternative “Avon Hills,” honoring local history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rochester_Hills%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Rochester Hills Museum, housed at Van Hoosen Farm, preserves over a century of local history and serves as the town’s cultural heart.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wonderfulmuseums.com/museum/rochester-hills-museum/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Van Hoosen Farm, the museum’s site, evolved from a frontier homestead into a modern museum, mirroring broader American historical shifts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wonderfulmuseums.com/museum/rochester-hills-museum/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Rochester Hills Public Library, part of the city’s services, also welcomes patrons from neighboring Rochester and Oakland Township under a shared agreement.",
